{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14818-so-what-exactly-is-a-lot-of-angels-for-the-godmachine-questions-on-scope","id":14818,"title":"So what exactly is a Lot of Angels for the Godmachine? Questions on Scope","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T12:06:22-08:00","id":14818,"title":"So what exactly is a Lot of Angels for the Godmachine? Questions on Scope","content":"So the book seems really ambiguous on the Numbers of Angels. Like what they consider a lot of angels would be. Sometime they say creating even one angel for certain tasks are a stretch of the resources, but for some situations (like bringing down Agencies) a bunch of Angels may be summoned. So what would be an actual major loss of Angels for the Godmachine? Say what would be considered enough angels wiped out to say clear a country like the US from Angel supervision for a time?<br /> <br /> How free is the Godmachine to send its agents across its various territories? I get the impression it is much more likely to send local agents against a traveling threat rather then dedicate say a single angel to it.<br /> <br /> How High in Rank do you think its Angels Go? Say the Godmachine is what Rank 9? Would that mean it could say have Rank 8 Angels?<br /> <br /> And How many Demons are there seems to be really open, but we have at least some indication. The book mentions Vampires outnumber Demons normally, so we can at least figure then that Demons are likely numbering less then a 100k on Earth... but that still an ambiguous number.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Godmachine is said to be able control the movement of Constellations if it needs to. So what the hell that is really up there in power. So my guess then is that the Godmachine is spread across multiple worlds. <br /> <br /> The Godmachine seems to simplify things by splitting things up into different scales and addressing things on each scale with only the appropriate amount of power. But in this way we may not really see the far hand of the Godmachine, as it uses only more local agents. But do Angels break that mold? Are angels, or angel components the one part of the Godmachine that it is willing to ship to whatever world it infects as its own resource?<br /> <br /> <br /> Since the Godmachine Seems to have fingers in some far off Cosmic Pies it actually can present the option of doing a plot that the Godmachine is dying, or a trend in the worlds that it infests that it is being rejected/resisted. If anyone ever read Ultimates, this is pretty much what was happening with the Chitauri when Earth repelled their invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T12:25:11-08:00","id":14827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14818-so-what-exactly-is-a-lot-of-angels-for-the-godmachine-questions-on-scope#post14818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How free is the Godmachine to send its agents across its various territories? I get the impression it is much more likely to send local agents against a traveling threat rather then dedicate say a single angel to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One account in the preview document tells of an angel which the God-Machine supposedly sent into outer space to stop an asteroid which would have otherwise wiped out humanity. However, bringing that single angel into existence required sacrificing thousands of mortals around the world, under the guise of wars and natural catastrophes, as well as &quot;a dozen more such sacrifices every hour for the weeks the angel required to complete its mission&quot;. So while technically the Machine may possess power on a galactic scale, the cost of wielding that might exceed the resources it has available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T12:28:31-08:00","id":14832,"title":"","content":"I didn't say it was free, one of the big themes is everything costs the Godmachine something. But the book said it literally could rearrange constellations, so that means it can conceivably has the resources to perform this feat, even if it say could only do it once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:28:33-08:00","id":30551,"title":"","content":"The Global Population of Angels is precisely one metric Plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T16:51:13-08:00","id":30643,"title":"","content":"So, I think it is deliberately ambiguous, so that the GM can tailor these factors as they need for their game without the CWoD problem of &quot;But but but it says in 'Lords of the outer floopadoop' that there are exactly 13008.5 were-aardvarks in existence&quot; that so plagued me, er I mean us, back in the old days.<br /> <br /> Over detailing things was always a problem in CWoD and I like when they avoid doing it in NWoD, and avoid giving definite 'Word of God' answers on mysteries. (VII is still my favorite example of how these things should be done)<br /> <br /> That said, it's generally implied that a Single Occult Matrix supports the continued existence in our world of 1 Angel, or a group of linked angels that function together so they may as well be one angel with multiple bodies...<br /> Haven't really gotten into the section on angels as antagonists in the Demon preview PDF yet, but I assume that an angel of a given rank is a matched opponent for a demon of similar Primum rating, and so a LOT of angels would be say one and a half to three angels per Demon in a given situation.<br /> <br /> Assume also that if Demons start trying to &quot;Clear Out&quot; an area killing off all the angels, that this is gonna trigger the G-Ms warning bells and result in large amounts of resources being sent there to clear things up.<br /> Given the scope of the God Machines powers, if all the demons on Earth conspired to Clear the USA of Angels, and bring down ALL G-M infrastructures in the states, the G-M would, more than likely simply decide that it was more trouble than it was worth, trigger some sort of fail-safe infrastructure hidden on the underside of the tectonic plates, detonate the super volcano under yellowstone and then sink America under the seas. Better to clear out the rabble if they all foolishly gather together, and it can always rebuild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:52:35-08:00","id":31137,"title":"","content":"I think that the GM would be a rank 10 being. as you said, the GM keeps the stars and galaxies in orbit, and can swing em around like slow motion poi if it needed to. Ive wondered the same thing on numbers before. Before Demon came out, i had even created a rank 1 mass produced angel type that had high enough numbers to be able to do regular patrols of a city. im not sure if this is viable anymore (though, it could be some swarm power of a greater angel that spreads its eyes around town). population of angels probably varies greatly. in my las vegas setting, angels are very rare because the foundational infrastructure of the area is tainted. i agree that it would be impossible to whipe out every angel in the country without activating the GM's failsafes (which could include sending a powerful archangel). a city would even be a big challenge, though one less likely to have such huge catastrophic results. of course, another good question is whether itd be a good idea. unless the demons are prepared to take over the roles of angels in keeping the natural forces at bay, i doubt itd be smart. angels do have benign tasks, such as keeping the aforemention supervolcano from going off, keeping vampires and mummies and Fae from causing widespread havok, etc. i doubt demons would be able to replace them effectively, so id foresee a lot of anarchy, as well as the slipping of the status quo (meaning Fae could start mass invasions, spirits pour out of the shadow, mummies awakening randomly due to backups in the sekhem flows, strix having little in their way, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T17:24:37-08:00","id":31346,"title":"","content":"The books leave it up to the storyteller to determine how much doomsday the Godmachine keeps at bay, but I would say removing its influence from an Area wouldn't mean instant doomsday, its just that at certain points in history it has averted some nasty disasters like Super Volcanoes and Meteors, but its not the only one doing this, we also have Werewolves, Incarnae, and Archmagi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}